  "visibleTextNormalized": "HomeContact us Contact us Want to learn more about our school, speak to someone, or raise a question or concern? We’re here to help. Contact us to: ask about enrolment or school costs arrange a visit before you enrol give feedback or raise a concern get involved as a parent or carer find out more about how we support students and families. Call, email or visit us Our office is open Monday to Friday 8.30am to 3.30pm during school term. fortstreet-h.school@det.nsw.edu.au (opens in new window) 8585 1600 (opens in new window) 620 PARRAMATTA ROAD, NSW 2049 PETERSHAM (Access via Palace Street) Location map We are located at 620 PARRAMATTA ROAD, NSW 2049 PETERSHAM (Access via Palace Street). Skip Google Map Check if you're in our local intake area Many NSW public schools have specific local intake areas. If you live inside a school’s local intake area, your child is guaranteed a place at that school. Use School Finder to find out if you live in our local intake area. Need an interpreter? The Telephone Interpreting Service allows parents and carers to connect with qualified interpreters by phoning 131 450 and requesting their language. This free and on-demand service facilitates clear communication between parents and schools. Parents and carers can listen to instructions on using the service in their language. Have a concern or feedback? We’re here to help. If you have a question, concern or want to share feedback, please email us. fortstreet-h.school@det.nsw.edu.au (opens in new window) Travel to school Learn about local transport options and how to get here safely. east Our community Discover ways to volunteer and help shape our school community. east Section navigation About us Contact us Learning and support Our community School life",
